      "sample_index": 2,
      "text": "Let's solve the given problem step by step.\n\nGiven the quadratic equation \\(x^2 - 63x + k = 0\\) with roots that are prime numbers, we can use Vieta's formulas. For a quadratic equation of the form \\(x^2 + bx + c = 0\\), if the roots are \\(p\\) and \\(q\\), then:\n1. The sum of the roots \\(p + q = -b\\).\n2. The product of the roots \\(pq = c\\).\n\nIn this problem, the quadratic equation is \\(x^2 - 63x + k = 0\\), so:\n1. \\(p + q = 63\\).\n2. \\(pq = k\\).\n\nSince \\(p\\) and \\(q\\) are prime numbers and their sum is 63, we need to identify pairs of prime numbers that add up to 63. Let's find these pairs:\n\n- \\(63 = 2 + 61\\)\n- \\(63 = 3 + 60\\) (60 is not prime)\n- \\(63 = 5 + 58\\) (58 is not prime)\n- \\(63 = 7 + 56\\) (56 is not prime)\n- \\(63 = 11 + 52\\) (52 is not prime)\n- \\(63 = 13 + 50\\) (50 is not prime)\n- \\(63 = 17 + 46\\) (46 is not prime)\n- \\(63 = 19 + 44\\) (44 is not prime)\n- \\(63 = 23 + 40\\) (40 is not prime)\n- \\(63 = 29 + 34\\) (34 is not prime)\n- \\(63 = 31 + 32\\) (32 is not prime)\n- \\(63 = 37 + 26\\) (26 is not prime)\n- \\(63 = 41 + 22\\) (22 is not prime)\n- \\(63 = 43 + 20\\) (20 is not prime)\n- \\(63 = 47 + 16\\) (16 is not prime)\n- \\(63 = 53 + 10\\) (10 is not prime)\n- \\(63 = 59 + 4\\) (4 is not prime)\n- \\(63 = 61 + 2\\) (The pair (61, 2) is valid since both 61 and 2 are prime numbers.)\n\nSo, the only valid pair of prime numbers that add up to 63 is \\(61\\) and \\(2\\). Therefore, the value of \\(k\\) is:\n\\[k = 61 \\cdot 2 = 122.\\]\n\nNow, let's check if there are any other possible values for \\(k\\). The only other way to express 63 as a sum of two prime numbers is:\n\\[63 = 63 + 0\\]\nbut since 0 is not a prime number, there are no other valid pairs.\n\nThus, the only possible value of \\(k\\) is 122. Therefore, the number of possible values of \\(k\\) is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{1}\n\\]\n\nLet's confirm this with a Python code implementation.\n```python\n# Function to check if a number is prime\r\ndef is_prime(n):\r\n    if n <= 1:\r\n        return False\r\n    if n == 2:\r\n        return True\r\n    if n % 2 == 0:\r\n        return False\r\n    for i in range(3, int(n**0.5) + 1, 2):\r\n        if n % i == 0:\r\n            return False\r\n    return True\r\n\r\n# Find all pairs of prime numbers that sum up to 63\r\nprime_pairs = []\r\nfor i in range(2, 63):\r\n    if is_prime(i) and is_prime(63 - i):\r\n        prime_pairs.append((i, 63 - i))\r\n\r\n# Calculate the possible values of k\r\npossible_ks = set(i * j for i, j in prime_pairs)\r\n\r\n# Number of possible values of k\r\nnumber_of_possible_values = len(possible_ks)\r\nprint((prime_pairs, possible_ks, number_of_possible_values))\n```",
